The judge check passed, so I've started the real probes: 8 cells are queued (the most one wake may submit), all still waiting for GPUs.

**Judge check: passed.** I re-ran the reference model on the 1,500 document questions. The judge accuracy (share of answers the Qwen3-8B judge accepts) came out .610, the same as the recorded run. All 1,500 answers were byte-identical, because decoding is greedy (always the most likely token). So when two runs differ later, the difference comes from the probe, not from noise.

**Queued, nothing measured yet** (start estimates 08:00–16:30; the judge check started much earlier than its estimate):

| Question | Cells (reference model, seed 42) | Training decision it feeds |
|---|---|---|
| Document loss: reading, page choice, or using the content? | answer after copying the evidence; correct page only; chosen page given uncompressed | add evidence-then-answer labels; send the chosen page uncompressed at serving |
| Text loss: no room to reason, or missing content? | plain long-chunk baseline (none existed for this model); evidence-then-answer | evidence-then-answer labels for text |
| Can the decoder's attention pick the right page better than the digit prompt, with no training? | attention re-runs on 10-page documents and on HotpotQA, then a CPU job combining the two scores | whether page-picking needs training |

**Problems found:**
- **The photo text-vs-pixels probe cannot run as planned.** The photo set has no OCR text (every row's document text is empty). It needs a new set of the 500 TextVQA questions with their OCR tokens. I marked the plan as wrong in CAMPAIGN.md (kept, not deleted) and pointed it at the new set.
- **The results page is empty.** `expmon display` shows 0 rows even though the grid lists the campaign's runs. I filed this as an expmon defect. Until it is fixed, results go to `docs/probe_campaign_2026-11.md`.

I also changed one rule in CAMPAIGN.md: probes that change what gets compressed (correct page only, a page left uncompressed) now report their slot count next to the result. Before, a slot total off by more than 1% marked a cell unhealthy.

**Next:** the next wake starts when the correct-page-only cell ends, or in 6 hours at most. It will compare finished cells against the baseline. Then it will submit the seed-43 repeats, the uncompressed-reader version of the text probe, and build the inputs for the long-chunk probe and the OCR set.

Nothing needed from you. Optional: clear the old alert about the 01:00 and 01:30 failed wakes; they hit the usage quota and need no fix.
